jobs.description:
Project is an AI company in the Healthcare space. It is rolling out an enterprise deployment of its AI platform for a major US healthcare insurance company, with delivery scheduled for mid\-September — so we're looking for someone who can join quickly and hit the ground running.

Engagement: Contractor, full\-time, initial 3 months with possible extension.

Location: US preferred; remote candidates outside the US with very strong FHIR expertise are also welcome.

**Your responsibilities will include:**

* Building integrations with existing healthcare systems and systems of record;
* Implementing and maintaining a large number of third\-party integrations;
* Customising the Anterior platform to the needs of a specific enterprise client;
* Working closely with the engineering team on a heavily customised enterprise deployment (not a typical SaaS rollout);
* Contributing from day one with minimal onboarding to help the team meet the mid\-September delivery deadline.

**What we expect from you:**

* 8–10 years of commercial software engineering experience;
* Strong hands\-on experience with FHIR;
* Proven experience building integrations in the healthcare domain;
* Experience with US healthcare insurance or US healthcare providers is a big plus;
* Ability to ramp up quickly and work independently without a long onboarding;
* Advanced English.

**We offer:**

* A high\-impact enterprise project with a leading Healthcare AI company;
* Remote work (US preferred, but strong FHIR candidates worldwide are considered);
* A fast, simple hiring process — just two steps: an intro call and a live coding interview.

**Please note: this is a contractor position; vacation and sick leave are not covered.**

Pay: $10,000\.00 \- $10,500\.00 per month

Work Location: In person
